        "filename": "Rainbow Row, Charleston SC 2016.07.14 (56).jpg",
        "caption": "Charleston is the oldest city in South Carolina dating back to its founding in 1670.   The city’s Rainbow Row houses date back to the 1700s.  They originally fronted the Cooper River.   Most of the buildings had no interior stairs limiting access between the first and second floorsto exterior stairs in the back yards.  A 1778 fire destroyed much of the neighborhood leaving only these houses on East Bay Street.",
